  "slug": "codes-distance-49c0",
  "summary": "Six preprints tie code design to hardware-level fault distance, via scheduling, flags, exact certification, and cultivation analysis.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is that effective distance under circuit-level noise, not nominal code distance, governs practical performance. Proxima optimizes syndrome-extraction scheduling using a DEM-based proximity metric, and the singlet-flag scheme restores circuit distance for shuttled qLDPC codes in silicon. Armillary qLDPC codes target fixed-connectivity superconducting hardware at rates above 1/2. QEDist provides exact distance certification for stabilizer codes, including fault distance. The color-code work proposes small distance-3 and 4 codes with proved rate optimality, and the cultivation analysis shows S-gate proxies overstate the fault distance of T-gate cultivation. New here is the emphasis on hardware-aware construction together with exact verification of fault distance.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
